  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Infrastructure</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia, through the Kokoda Initiative Partnership (KIP), is working closely with the Northern and Central Provincial Governments of Papua New Guinea to improve infrastructure for communities that live alongside the historic Kokoda Track. Australia&#x2019;s support focuses on improving health, education, water, sanitation, and law enforcement services&#x2014;while also boosting local employment.
&#x200d;
Key achievements include the construction of two new water catchment facilities and the upgrade of two gravity-fed water systems in four villages, benefiting more than 1,100 people in track communities. Australia also supported the installation of sanitation facilities at 96 guesthouses and campsites, directly improving hygiene and tourism services for visitors. In partnership with the Central Provincial Government and Seventh Day Adventist Health Services, a health aid post was reopened in 2024, now serving more than 1,000 people from seven villages.
&#x200d;
To maintain law and order, three dual-purpose police and Kokoda Track Authority patrol houses were upgraded. These projects created more than 210 local jobs, for both men and women, as builders, cooks, porters, security, and support workers.
&#x200d;
Australia&#x2019;s investment in these projects demonstrates a strong commitment to sustainable development in the Kokoda region&#x2014;improving community access to essential services while strengthening the local economy through job creation and tourism support.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2024-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2025-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
